Input: {"question": "Which person or organization did Mirjam Ekstedt work for?", "source_segments": {"D1S1": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 0, "end": 80, "text": "Title: The Academic Pursuits of Mirjam Ekstedt: A Linnaeus University Connection"}, "D1S2": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 82, "end": 242, "text": "In the quaint town of Växjö, Sweden, nestled between the tranquil lakes and lush forests, lies Linnaeus University, a hub of academic excellence and innovation."}, "D1S3": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 243, "end": 416, "text": "It is here that our story begins, one that delves into the professional life of Mirjam Ekstedt, a researcher whose work has left an indelible mark on the academic community."}, "D1S4": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 417, "end": 542, "text": "Mirjam Ekstedt, a scholar of great repute, has spent a significant portion of her career affiliated with Linnaeus University."}, "D1S5": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 543, "end": 721, "text": "This affiliation is not merely a passing association, but rather a deep-seated connection that has shaped her research and contributed to the university's rich academic heritage."}, "D1S6": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 722, "end": 846, "text": "One of the earliest indications of Ekstedt's connection to Linnaeus University can be traced back to her publication record."}, "D1S7": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 847, "end": 1020, "text": "A thorough examination of her research papers and articles reveals a consistent affiliation with the university, with many of her works bearing the Linnaeus University logo."}, "D1S8": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1021, "end": 1229, "text": "For instance, her 2015 paper, \"Exploring the Intersection of Technology and Education,\" published in the Journal of Educational Research, clearly lists her as a researcher affiliated with Linnaeus University."}, "D1S9": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1230, "end": 1364, "text": "This pattern of affiliation is consistent across multiple publications, providing strong evidence of her connection to the university."}, "D1S10": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1365, "end": 1549, "text": "Further investigation into Ekstedt's academic background reveals that she has been an active participant in various research projects and initiatives undertaken by Linnaeus University."}, "D1S11": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1550, "end": 1737, "text": "One such project, \"Enhancing Digital Literacy in the Classroom,\" was a collaborative effort between the university's Department of Education and the Swedish National Agency for Education."}, "D1S12": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1738, "end": 1918, "text": "Ekstedt's involvement in this project, as a lead researcher, demonstrates her integral role in shaping the university's research agenda and contributing to its academic excellence."}, "D1S13": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1919, "end": 2049, "text": "In addition to her research endeavors, Ekstedt has also been involved in teaching and mentoring activities at Linnaeus University."}, "D1S14": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2050, "end": 2222, "text": "Her profile on the university's website lists her as a lecturer in the Department of Education, where she has taught courses on educational technology and research methods."}, "D1S15": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2223, "end": 2392, "text": "This involvement in teaching and mentoring further solidifies her connection to the university, highlighting her commitment to nurturing the next generation of scholars."}, "D1S16": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2393, "end": 2497, "text": "The university's own records and publications also provide compelling evidence of Ekstedt's affiliation."}, "D1S17": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2498, "end": 2697, "text": "The Linnaeus University Annual Report for 2018, for instance, features Ekstedt as one of the university's prominent researchers, highlighting her work on digital literacy and its impact on education."}, "D2S1": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 0, "end": 14, "text": "Mirjam Ekstedt"}, "D2S2": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 16, "end": 165, "text": "Mirjam Ekstedt is a renowned researcher in the field of interdisciplinary studies, best known for her groundbreaking work at the University of Tokyo."}, "D2S3": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 166, "end": 190, "text": "Early Life and Education"}, "D2S4": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 192, "end": 259, "text": "Mirjam Ekstedt was born on February 12, 1975, in Stockholm, Sweden."}, "D2S5": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 260, "end": 379, "text": "She pursued her undergraduate degree in sociology from the University of Stockholm, graduating magna cum laude in 1997."}, "D2S6": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 380, "end": 457, "text": "Ekstedt then moved to Japan to pursue her graduate studies, earning her Ph.D."}, "D2S7": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 458, "end": 520, "text": "in cultural anthropology from the University of Tokyo in 2003."}, "D2S8": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 521, "end": 527, "text": "Career"}, "D2S9": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 529, "end": 645, "text": "Ekstedt's academic career began at the University of Tokyo, where she worked as a research fellow from 2003 to 2006."}, "D2S10": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 646, "end": 734, "text": "During this period, she collaborated with prominent scholars in the field, including Dr."}, "D2S11": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 735, "end": 800, "text": "Hiroshi Matsumoto, a leading expert in Japanese cultural studies."}, "D2S12": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 801, "end": 959, "text": "Ekstedt's research focused on the intersection of technology and society, with a particular emphasis on the impact of digital media on Japanese youth culture."}, "D2S13": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 960, "end": 1147, "text": "In 2006, Ekstedt published her seminal paper, \"The Virtual Self: An Exploration of Identity Formation in Online Communities,\" which was widely cited and praised by the academic community."}, "D2S14": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1148, "end": 1259, "text": "This work was instrumental in establishing Ekstedt as a leading authority in the field of digital anthropology."}, "D2S15": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1260, "end": 1280, "text": "Studies and Research"}, "D2S16": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1282, "end": 1377, "text": "Ekstedt's research at the University of Tokyo was marked by several notable studies, including:"}, "D2S17": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1379, "end": 1560, "text": "* \"The Tokyo Youth Project\" (2004-2005): A comprehensive study on the impact of digital media on the lives of Japanese youth, which was funded by the Japanese Ministry of Education."}, "D2S18": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1561, "end": 1756, "text": "* \"The Virtual Village\" (2005-2006): An ethnographic study of online communities in Japan, which explored the ways in which digital technologies shape social relationships and cultural practices."}, "D2S19": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1757, "end": 1767, "text": "References"}, "D2S20": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1769, "end": 1782, "text": "* Ekstedt, M."}, "D2S21": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1783, "end": 1790, "text": "(2006)."}, "D2S22": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1791, "end": 1868, "text": "The Virtual Self: An Exploration of Identity Formation in Online Communities."}, "D2S23": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1869, "end": 1913, "text": "Journal of Digital Anthropology, 1(1), 1-15."}, "D2S24": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1914, "end": 1944, "text": "* Matsumoto, H., & Ekstedt, M."}, "D2S25": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1945, "end": 1952, "text": "(2005)."}, "D2S26": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1953, "end": 2007, "text": "The Impact of Digital Media on Japanese Youth Culture."}, "D2S27": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 2008, "end": 2052, "text": "Journal of Japanese Studies, 27(2), 123-145."}, "D2S28": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 2053, "end": 2075, "text": "* University of Tokyo."}, "D2S29": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 2076, "end": 2083, "text": "(2006)."}, "D2S30": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 2084, "end": 2121, "text": "Research Fellowships: Mirjam Ekstedt."}}, "candidates": [{"candidate_id": "C0", "answer": "Linnaeus University", "card_ids": ["d1:c0"]}], "original_cards": [{"doc_id": "d1", "card_id": "d1:c0", "entity": "Mirjam Ekstedt", "scope": "organization", "claim": "Mirjam Ekstedt worked for Linnaeus University.", "answer": "Linnaeus University", "quote": "Mirjam Ekstedt, a scholar of great repute, has spent a significant portion of her career affiliated with Linnaeus University. This affiliation is not merely a passing association, but rather a deep-seated connection that has shaped her research and contributed to the university's rich academic heritage. One of the earliest indications of Ekstedt's connection to Linnaeus University can be traced back to her publication record. A thorough examination of her research papers and articles reveals a consistent affiliation with the university, with many of her works bearing the Linnaeus University logo. For instance, her 2015 paper, \"Exploring the Intersection of Technology and Education,\" published in the Journal of Educational Research, clearly lists her as a researcher affiliated with Linnaeus University. This pattern of affiliation is consistent across multiple publications, providing strong evidence of her connection to the university. Further investigation into Ekstedt's academic background reveals that she has been an active participant in various research projects and initiatives undertaken by Linnaeus University. One such project, \"Enhancing Digital Literacy in the Classroom,\" was a collaborative effort between the university's Department of Education and the Swedish National Agency for Education. Ekstedt's involvement in this project, as a lead researcher, demonstrates her integral role in shaping the university's research agenda and contributing to its academic excellence. In addition to her research endeavors, Ekstedt has also been involved in teaching and mentoring activities at Linnaeus University. Her profile on the university's website lists her as a lecturer in the Department of Education, where she has taught courses on educational technology and research methods.", "original_document_number": 1}], "initial_answers": ["Linnaeus University", "University of Tokyo"]}
